review:
Update to my first review. I give 2 stars ONLY for the user base and bodies of water database it has. Otherwise the app is complete trash. I would love to give it 1 star because of how annoying the apps lack of features and technical merit are but thats probably unfair. I still would not recommend actually purchasing the paid version. 

The AI is still awful - cant even identify a spadefish correctly;
The gear database is still beyond horrid. Half of my gear which is all basically new stuff doesnt appear in the database and I cant for the life of me figure out if you can add it or not manually;
I still have to endure a gazillion freshwater largemouth bass photos everybday in my feed that I donΓÇÖt want (I fish saltwater) and have tried everything to be rid of;
Still no tidal forecast;
The fishing species bite times forecaster is still useless (was laughing about it with another angler at the pier yesterday).   

The ONLY things this app has going for it are itΓÇÖs large user base and the large body of water database it has. I suspect this will eventually have some sort of ad endurace value to it someday because I dont know any other fishing app that has the user base or water body data. Otherwise I am at a total loss for what they are doing with the VC funding they keep getting because the app isnt getting any better on a technical basis. Seriously, at this point its not that difficult to train AWS rekongnition to get your identification to a better percentage than ZERO (it has literally never identified a fish correctly for me).

Update! It has been one year since I wrote the review below and things seem to be improving (bumped from one star to three
). I am however, still seeing a ton of bass posts and I donΓÇÖt even fish for bass; not following the species, or a ΓÇ£catch positionΓÇ¥ where they can even be caught. Then thereΓÇÖs the premium features: which are minimal considering the cost. I definitely recommend this app to any and all anglers and I hope things continue to improve. Still has a lot of potential!

App has taken a turn for the worst, crap from other countries is showing up in my feed, have to scroll for days to even find a catch in the places I fish not to mention every species known to man is also showing up in my feed; app has potential but doesn't seem to be getting the attention it needs!
